# Regression: the pre-existing bare no-paren closure-literal shorthand,
# MULTI-LINE block form (`x:` followed by an indented block), must still
# work exactly as before when `x` is not a declared callable at all --
# this is the resolution redesign's row-4 fallback (see
# src/desugar_array_block.rs's module doc comment). Uses a `let` inside
# the block to prove the body is parsed with the fully general statement
# grammar (not a restricted "one collectible item per line" grammar)
# regardless of which interpretation it ends up resolving to.

def main():
    let f = n:
        let doubled = n * 2
        doubled + 1
    print f(5)
